value patch → computed property","level":3,"type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Add"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Transition\/interpolate"},{"type":"text","text":", and other pure-function patches carry no state."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"They fan an input through math and emit an output. In SwiftUI that’s a computed"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"property (or an inline expression) — no ","type":"text"},{"code":"@State","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", no side effect.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Interaction-%E2%86%92-gesture-+-State","level":3,"type":"heading","text":"Interaction → gesture + `@State`"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Origami’s Interaction patch exposes discrete output ports: "},{"code":"down","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"position","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":","},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"onTap","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"onDoubleTap","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"onLongPress","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":". Each maps to a SwiftUI gesture recognizer"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"whose output lands in "},{"code":"@State","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" or fires a callback. The "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/samatwork.Swami\/documentation\/Swami\/Interaction","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" helper"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"attaches only the recognizer for each output the caller requests, which keeps"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"gesture arbitration clean."}]},{"anchor":"Statememory-%E2%86%92-State-+-update-logic","level":3,"type":"heading","text":"State\/memory → `@State` + update logic"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Switch"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Sample and Hold"},{"type":"text","text":" remember a value across evaluations. That’s what"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@State"},{"type":"text","text":" is for. Codegen emits the state variable plus the update path (a gesture"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"callback, a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".onChange"},{"type":"text","text":", or an assignment inside a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"withAnimation"},{"type":"text","text":" block)."}]},{"anchor":"Animation-%E2%86%92-withAnimation--animation","level":3,"type":"heading","text":"Animation → `withAnimation` \/ `.animation`"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"Classic Animation","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"Pop Animation","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", and other animation patches drive a value","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"toward a target over time. In SwiftUI, that’s a state change wrapped in","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"withAnimation","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" or an ","type":"text"},{"code":".animation(_:value:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" modifier on the animated property.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Continuous-time springs that don’t have a stock SwiftUI equivalent get flagged","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"by the parser — Swami won’t fake them.","type":"text"}]},{"anchor":"Flag-dont-fake","level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Flag, don’t fake"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Some Origami semantics don’t have a SwiftUI equivalent. When the parser hits one,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"it emits a marker in the IR and codegen surfaces the gap rather than papering over","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"it. The current list: continuous-time springs, custom JavaScript patches,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"absolute-position layout.","type":"text"}]}],"kind":"content"}],"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"major":0,"patch":0},"references":{"doc://samatwork.Swami/documentation/Swami/Drag":{"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Drag"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"SwiftUI equivalent of Origami’s "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"Drag","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" patch ("},{"code":"origami.Drag","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":")."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/samatwork.Swami\/documentation\/Swami\/Drag","title":"Drag","url":"\/documentation\/swami\/drag","role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Drag"}]},"doc://samatwork.Swami/documentation/Swami/Interaction":{"fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Interaction","kind":"identifier"}],"kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Interaction","kind":"identifier"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/samatwork.Swami\/documentation\/Swami\/Interaction","role":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"SwiftUI equivalent of Origami’s ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Interaction"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" patch.","type":"text"}],"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/swami\/interaction","title":"Interaction"},"doc://samatwork.Swami/documentation/Swami/Beats":{"type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The four-beat discipline that keeps the translator honest: one pattern per branch,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"compile-clean before opening a PR, visual gate against Origami’s own render, ship","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"only on Reviewer approval plus a human spot-check.","type":"text"}],"role":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/samatwork.Swami\/documentation\/Swami\/Beats","title":"Beats","kind":"article","url":"\/documentation\/swami\/beats"},"doc://samatwork.Swami/documentation/Swami":{"url":"\/documentation\/swami","abstract":[{"text":"An Origami → SwiftUI translator: a deterministic parser reads Facebook’s ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".origami"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"patch graph into a semantic IR, and a codegen writes that IR out as SwiftUI. Swami","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"is also the patch-matched helper library that fills gaps between Origami patches","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"and native SwiftUI — one helper per Origami patch, named after the patch, sized by","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Origami’s patch surface. Every pattern that lands is a deliverable, verified against","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Origami’s own render, and shipped as a DocC-embedded example.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/samatwork.Swami\/documentation\/Swami","title":"Swami","kind":"symbol","role":"collection","type":"topic"}}}